The provided class `SingleDoOnError` is a thin wrapper around an existing `SingleSource` that merely adds a side‑effect on error propagation. Its logic consists of delegating calls to the downstream observer and invoking a user‑provided `Consumer` in the `onError` path. The implementation does not contain any computationally intensive work, complex state management, or algorithmic variations that would benefit from micro‑benchmarking. Consequently, a JMH benchmark would not yield meaningful performance insights beyond the inherent overhead of the RxJava infrastructure, which is already covered by existing RxJava benchmarks. Therefore, generating a dedicated JMH test for this specific operator is unnecessary.